;==============================================================================
;NOTE: This program is written for and compiled with Eric Isaacson's A86
;      assembly language compiler, using Options +P2 -F (80286 CPU
;      with no FPU).
;==============================================================================





;Change INT 70h code in all programs that use it (SCANCODE, JOYKEYS,
;  MOUSKEYS, SLOWDOWN, etc.)

;Add external function to BIOS (INT 15h, AX = C230h-C23xh, BX/ES:[BX] as
;  params, return AX/BX/CX/DX, to send fake mouse data.  Need button press,
;  button release, button press & release, button double-click, move mouse
;  (# pixels in graphics mode, # characters in text mode), click wheel,
;  install check.

;Horizontal Wheel: Right = Increment by 2, Left = Decrement by 2.  Verify!

;Get/Set Mouse BIOS Data in XBDA!  (Copy from PS2MTest)

;Need separate scaling factors per mouse.  Wireless Mouse in much more
;  sensitive than wired mouse.  Allow slow-down of many times (up to 16 or so).

;Not reading Environment right away??  SET Resolution:8, run USBMOUSE, says
;  resolution is still 4.  Run it again, it says 8.  Happens because we
;  display status before we call ChangeRates if already in memory (things
;  have changed, but we're not displaying the updated status).

;IntelliMouse2 protocol = IntelliMouse Explorer Mouse

;HW Emulation doesn't work at all, even with CTMOUS19.  Fix it or remove it.
;Handle DisableAll
;Have "HorizontalWheelTrigger" button.  This will handle GE Mouse, and
;  also allow horizontal scrolling with a single wheel.
;Is our beeping/keyboard problem related to IRQ priorities?  If so, we
;  may not be able to do hardware emulation at all unless the USB IRQ
;  has a lower priority than IRQ 12??
;If HW emulation, show status because there MAY be a PS2 Mouse
;Resolution doesn't have any effect, at least in HW emulation
;Beeping not a problem if no USB Mice are attached.
;  Need to monitor MouseChangeCode closely to see what's happening.
;When doing HW Emulation, handle Resolution & Scaling Properly
;Take Over INT 9 when simulating Mouse Movements?  Disable Speaker at same time?
;When emulating HW, Keyboard slows down, beeps, repeat keys don't work.
;Need to Disable Keyboard when emulating w/ Method 2 or 3?
;  If not, since both Mouse and Keyboard use Port 60h, we could have problems.
;Sometimes SEVERELY slows down keyboard, at least in hardware emulation mode
;   Method 3 on laptop
;Doesn't work on Desktop with Method 2 or 3.  Find out why.  May need to
;  do a Trace.
;If emulating HW, disabling PS2 Mouse doesn't do anything.  Need to handle
;  appropriately in Status.
;Verify unused code with +x Option
;Add API similar to USBKEYB to move mouse/press buttons?
;Add support for Keyboard keys also, not just system keys.  Saw a reference
;  to a Mouse that does that.
;Make sure Wheels Option gets handled properly when changing from
;  BIOS to HW emulation (or vice versa), especially of BIOS Option
;  occurs after Wheel Option on command-line.
;May need special handling if USBUHCI uses IRQ 8 or 12.
;Test everything (including "adding" PS/2+USB Mice) since we've changed
;  how everything works
;Order of Axes on GE Mouse is X, Y, Wheel, Z (not X, Y, Z, Wheel).  Find out
;  exactly how it works and make it compatible.  Order is the same on
;  the HP wireless mouse, even though it doesn't have a second wheel and
;  the wheel doesn't move sideways.
;Convert Keyboard Codes (DisableMouse, DisableKeyboard, etc.) to EQUates
;If using Hardware emulation, we don't want to reset the PS2 Mouse when
;  installing.  We also may need to warn user if they use us to Reset
;  the PS2 Mouse the INT 33h driver will stop working.
;Only allow BIOS Option on initial install?  If not, we will need to test
;  if we actually changed it.  If we switched from BIOS to Hardware, we'll
;  need to transfer the INT 33h caller address to the real BIOS, and purge
;  our PS2 Mouse Entry.  If swi